5. Update web.xml for Servlet Mapping
Make sure the web.xml file in the WEB-INF folder maps the servlet to a URL pattern.

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<web-app xmlns="http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee 
                             http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee/web-app_3_0.xsd"
         version="3.0">
    <servlet>
        <servlet-name>userServlet</servlet-name>
        <servlet-class>com.example.UserServlet</servlet-class>
    </servlet>
    <servlet-mapping>
        <servlet-name>userServlet</servlet-name>
        <url-pattern>/UserServlet</url-pattern>
    </servlet-mapping>
</web-app>

6. Install JSTL Library for <c:forEach>
The c:forEach tag used in userList.jsp is part of the JSTL (JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library). Ensure you add JSTL to your project if it is not already included.

You can add the JSTL library by including it in your WEB-INF/lib folder:

jstl-1.2.jar
standard-1.1.2.jar

Alternatively, you can add the JSTL dependencies if using Maven:

<dependency>
    <groupId>javax.servlet.jsp.jstl</groupId>
    <artifactId>jstl</artifactId>
    <version>1.2</version>
</dependency>

7. Run the Application
1-Compile the Java classes and deploy the project to a servlet container like Apache Tomcat.
2-Run the application by accessing the servlet in the browser:
http://localhost:8080/YourWebAppName/UserServlet
This should display a list of users in an HTML table, which was passed from the UserServlet to the userList.jsp.

Explanation of Flow:
1-UserServlet receives the HTTP GET request and calls the UserManager to fetch a list of users.
2-The servlet sets the list of users as a request attribute and forwards the request to userList.jsp.
3-userList.jsp accesses the list of users from the request and uses the <c:forEach> tag to iterate over the list and display the user information in an HTML table.
4-The JSTL <c:forEach> tag dynamically generates the rows for each user in the table.





